### Topic 40 - JPA Relationships (VS Code "REST Client" extension)
@base = http://localhost:8080/api

### Product catalogue
GET {{base}}/products

### Customers (summary DTO, loaded with @EntityGraph - 1 SQL statement)
GET {{base}}/customers

### One customer with address, orders and products (DTOs)
GET {{base}}/customers/1

### Same customer returned as the ENTITY (@JsonManagedReference / @JsonBackReference / @JsonIgnore)
GET {{base}}/customers/1/raw

########## N+1 demos - compare "sqlStatements" and watch the console ##########

### N+1 problem: 1 + 3 + 3 = 7 statements
GET {{base}}/customers/demo/n-plus-one

### Fix 1: JOIN FETCH -> 1 statement
GET {{base}}/customers/demo/join-fetch

### Fix 2: @EntityGraph -> 1 statement
GET {{base}}/customers/demo/entity-graph

### LazyInitializationException on purpose
GET {{base}}/customers/demo/lazy-error/1

########## Writing through relationships ##########

### Create a customer + address with ONE save (cascade)
POST {{base}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dina Shah",
  "email": "dina@example.com",
  "address": { "street": "1 Main St", "city": "Pune", "zipCode": "411001", "country": "India" }
}

### Place an order for customer 4 with products 1 and 4 (fills the join table)
POST {{base}}/customers/4/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productIds": [1, 4] }

### Unknown product -> 400
POST {{base}}/customers/4/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productIds": [1, 77] }

### Remove order 2 from customer 1 (orphanRemoval -> DELETE)
DELETE {{base}}/customers/1/orders/2

### Delete customer 2 (cascade: address + orders deleted, products kept)
DELETE {{base}}/customers/2
